    "text": "The persistent dynamic object memory is initialized from visual observation at the first frame.",
    "topic": "memory initialization"
  },
  {
    "text": "After initialization, the memory propagates object states for multiple time steps without requiring any further visual input.",
    "topic": "memory propagation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Optional visual observations at subsequent frames can be used to update and correct the memory, but are not mandatory for state propagation.",
    "topic": "memory updates"
  },
  {
    "text": "The memory eliminates the need for continuous visual observation at every time step, not all visual observation indefinitely.",
    "topic": "visual observation dependency"
  }
